cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or the accompanying code, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "Rongcheng Jingtu Multi-Destination Route Planning Dataset: Distance and Air-Quality Matrices, Optimal Routes, and Benchmark Results"
abstract: >-
  Research data, source code and experiment scripts for a health-aware
  multi-destination route planning system that optimises a bi-objective cost
  combining driving distance and air-quality exposure. The dataset includes
  distance and AQI exposure matrices for instance sizes n = 5, 8, 10, 12 and 15,
  optimal routes produced by state-compressed dynamic programming (SCDP),
  Greedy and genetic algorithm baselines, raw measurements behind the reported
  tables, weight-sensitivity sweeps, and the hardware environment snapshot.
  Fixed random seeds and reproduction commands are documented in README.md and
  experiments/README.md.
